cheats={1:[('Authentication','Verify a claimed identity or origin; authorization decides access.'),('Hash / digest','A hash maps arbitrary input to a fixed-size output. It is not reversible encryption.'),('Integrity vs authentication','A trusted digest can detect changes; use a suitable MAC or signature for authenticated integrity.'),('MD4 / MD5 / SHA-1','Historical algorithms with collision weaknesses; do not choose them for new collision-resistant security.'),('SHA-1 dimensions','512-bit input blocks; five 32-bit state words; 80 rounds; 160-bit digest.'),('SHA-1 padding','Append 1 bit, enough zero bits, then the original length as a 64-bit value.'),('Schedule correction','W[t] = ROTL1(W[t−3] XOR W[t−8] XOR W[t−14] XOR W[t−16]).'),('First-round function','(B AND C) OR ((NOT B) AND D).'),('Worked example','Message 1a7fd53b4c is 40 bits. Its first new A is ba346dee; new C is 7bf36ae2.')],2:[('Avalanche effect','A small input change causes a substantial change in output.'),('Controlled test','Change one bit; keep algorithm, key, encoding, mode, IV and padding fixed as applicable.'),('Bit count','XOR equal-length outputs and count the 1 bits.'),('Hexadecimal','One hex digit = 4 bits; 32 hex digits = 128 bits.'),('Percentage','Changed bits ÷ compared output bits × 100.'),('Slide correction','The printed values differ by 30/128 = 23.4375%; first block alone is 30/64 = 46.875%.'),('50% expectation','About half the bits change on average in an idealized response; single trials can vary.'),('Security assessment','Use many trials and cryptanalysis. Avalanche and randomness tests alone do not prove security.')]} 
